# The lifecycle of each demo with a development route, in one scratch
# repository each: a pull request on branch development, its native merge,
# the service development snapshot dispatched on the merged main, then a
# signed release request from it. The development route is a service
# snapshot of the demo's own declaration through the harness's service
# development workflow; a demo whose declaration the snapshot planner refuses
# is refused before anything is created (docs/live-campaigns.md, Lifecycle).
# The profile: public, Buildah, native linux/amd64, the contract's
# container/readiness runner. Prepare with forgejo=<this file> and one
# job-image=<flavor>:<reviewed local image> per flavour named here;
# CI_JOB_IMAGE is the nanolinter image of the demo's toolchain flavour, which
# the demo's lint and build jobs run in and the snapshot builds the demo's
# producers in (none for the container-first Cargo service). amd64 runners
# only for now.
#
#   just campaign-lane <dir> forgejo test/live/campaigns/lifecycle-forgejo.cases
setting visibility=public
setting image-builder=buildah
setting admin-lint=false
setting admin-vulnerabilities=false
setting admin-application-tests=false
setting admin-reproducible-builds=false

consumer hello-maven-service lifecycle CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_JAVA CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=buildah RELEASE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64
consumer hello-cargo-container lifecycle CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_RUST CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=buildah RELEASE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64
